<li><strong><code>fetch(request, env)</code>:</strong> Main controller. It validates input, creates IDs, and runs the full workflow.</li>
<li><strong><code>createNeonBranch(...)</code>:</strong> Provisions an isolated Neon branch and returns a branch-specific <code>DATABASE_URL</code>.</li>
<li><strong><code>runClaude(...)</code>:</strong> Executes Claude Code inside the sandbox with your task and guardrail system prompt. In this example, <code>haiku</code> is used as the model, but you can choose any <a class="group inline" href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">supported model<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> like <code>sonnet</code> or <code>opus</code> depending on your needs. Change the <code>--model</code> flag accordingly.</li>
<li><strong><code>IS_SANDBOX</code> environment variable:</strong> Setting <code>IS_SANDBOX</code> to <code>&quot;1&quot;</code> grants Claude Code permission to execute commands that are normally restricted. Because the sandbox and database branch are entirely isolated, the agent can safely perform destructive actions with full autonomy, posing zero risk to your production environment.</li>
<li><strong><code>createPR(...)</code>:</strong> Uses GitHub CLI to open a PR and returns the PR URL.</li>
</ul><p>End-to-end flow (<strong>HTTP request -&gt; PR</strong>):</p><ol>
<li>Receive a <code>POST</code> request with <code>repoUrl</code> and <code>task</code>.</li>
<li>Create a unique <code>agentId</code>, sandbox instance, and Neon branch.</li>
<li>Clone the repository and create a git branch named after <code>agentId</code>.</li>
<li>Inject environment variables (<code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>, branch <code>DATABASE_URL</code>) and run Claude.</li>
<li>Commit and push the agent&#x27;s changes.</li>
<li>Create a Pull Request and return a JSON response with logs plus the PR link.</li>
</ol></div></li><li class="numbered-step relative mt-8! mb-0! flex w-full items-start gap-4 pl-0! before:flex before:size-7 before:items-center before:justify-center before:rounded-full before:bg-gray-new-20 before:text-center before:font-mono before:text-sm before:leading-snug before:font-medium before:tracking-tight before:text-white before:content-[counter(section)] before:[counter-increment:section] after:absolute after:top-8 after:-bottom-7 after:left-[.8125rem] after:w-px after:bg-gray-new-90 first:mt-0! last:after:bottom-0 dark:before:bg-gray-new-90 dark:before:text-black-pure dark:after:bg-gray-new-30 [&amp;_h2]:text-2xl [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal!"><div class="w-[calc(100%-100px)] flex-1 [&amp;&gt;*_*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:pt-0 md:[&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><h2 id="step-7-deploy-the-cloud-agent-runner-to-cloudflare" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Step 7: Deploy the cloud agent runner to Cloudflare</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#step-7-deploy-the-cloud-agent-runner-to-cloudflare" aria-label="Link to Step 7: Deploy the cloud agent runner to Cloudflare"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><p>Deploy your Worker to Cloudflare by running the following command in your terminal:</p><figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-